{
  "id": "https://m-lancini.github.io/frida-vocab/dictionary/caregiver",
  "type": "Concept",
  "prefLabel": {
    "en": "caregiver"
  },
  "definition": {
    "en": "Someone who provides ongoing care or support to a person who needs assistance because of age, illness, or disability, whether paid or unpaid."
  },
  "scopeNote": {
    "en": [
      "In both legal and philosophical debate, caregiving in the context of disability has shifted from a dependency narrative to a relational and empowerment-based view. The EU legal framework recognises carers’ rights through equality, employment, and social protection law,particularly via the Work–Life Balance Directive and the Court of Justice’s Coleman case"
    ]
  },
  "notation": [
    "1.3.1"
  ],
